  'lx.steps': '{n} steps', 'lx.rulesTab': 'Strategy by rule set',
  'lpn.ex': 'From here it is a fight for extra turns and a test of patience: do not hand over too many seeds.',
  'ls.n_open.title': 'Normal: the opening', 'ls.n_open.sub': 'The main line is pit 3 → pit 6', 'ls.n_open.goal': 'Find the best opening move.',
  'ls.n_open.intro': '<p>In Normal too, the best start is <b>pit 3</b> (its 4 seeds reach the store exactly: <b>extra turn</b>), followed by <b>pit 6</b>, according to deep engine analysis.</p><p>A Normal capture leaves the last seed in its pit, so it takes one seed less than in Kalah. That makes <b>the number of extra turns</b> and <b>not giving the opponent exact pits</b> even more important early on. Step through the line below with ← →.</p>',
  'ls.n_open.why': 'Pit {m} is the best opening move (deep engine analysis).', 'ls.n_open.hint': 'A pit that reaches the store exactly comes first. Otherwise, a move that gives the opponent no extra turn.',
  'ls.n_chain.title': 'Normal: extra-turn chains', 'ls.n_chain.sub': 'The order of extra turns', 'ls.n_chain.goal': 'Find the best move — it starts with an extra turn.',
  'ls.n_chain.intro': '<p>Sowing a pit that reaches the store exactly gives an <b>extra turn</b>. Using the pits <b>closest to the store first</b> keeps the farther pits exact, so the chain lasts longer.</p><p>Sow a far pit first and a nearer pit may get one seed too many. In a chain, order is everything.</p>',
  'ls.n_chain.why': 'Pit {m} is best: the first move of a sequence that starts with an extra turn.', 'ls.n_chain.hint': 'Compare each pit’s seeds with its distance to the store, starting nearest the store.',
  'ls.n_end.title': 'Normal: endgame', 'ls.n_end.sub': 'Exactly solved', 'ls.n_end.goal': 'Endgame: which move leaves the biggest final margin?',
  'ls.n_end.intro': '<p>The Normal endgame is about <b>counting</b>: 25 seeds win. A capture leaves the last seed in its pit, so count <b>on whose side that seed is when the game ends</b>.</p><p>The game ends the moment one side is empty, and the seeds left belong to the owner of each side. All values are exact.</p>',
  'ls.n_end.why': 'Pit {m} is the best move by exact analysis.', 'ls.n_end.hint': 'Add up extra turns, captures and the seeds left at the end.',
  'ls.e_open.title': 'Easy: the opening', 'ls.e_open.sub': 'Without captures, extra turns rule', 'ls.e_open.goal': 'Find the best opening move.',
  'ls.e_open.intro': '<p>In Easy too, the best start is <b>pit 3</b> for an extra turn, followed by <b>pit 6</b>, by deep analysis.</p><p>With no captures, the opening is decided mostly by <b>the number of extra turns</b> and <b>how you hand over seeds</b>. Avoid giving the opponent exact pits. Step through the line below with ← →.</p>',
  'ls.e_open.why': 'Pit {m} is the best opening move (deep engine analysis).', 'ls.e_open.hint': 'A pit that reaches the store exactly comes first; next, a move that gives the opponent no extra turn.',
  'ls.e_block.title': 'Easy: kill extra turns', 'ls.e_block.sub': 'Spoil the opponent’s exact pits', 'ls.e_block.goal': 'Find the best move that stops the opponent’s extra turns.',
  'ls.e_block.intro': '<p>Without captures, the opponent’s <b>extra turns</b> are the biggest threat. Drop one seed into such a pit and its count <b>no longer fits</b>: the extra turn is gone.</p><p>Count which of the opponent’s pits your move reaches and choose a move that takes extra turns away.</p>',
  'ls.e_block.why': 'Pit {m} takes extra turns away from the opponent.', 'ls.e_block.hint': 'Red rings mark the opponent’s pits that reach the store exactly now. Drop a seed there.',
  'ls.s_defend.title': 'Sunka: defence', 'ls.s_defend.sub': 'Guard against relay captures', 'ls.s_defend.goal': 'Find the best move against the opponent’s capture threat.',
  'ls.s_defend.intro': '<p>In Sunka, relays mean <b>unexpected piles can be captured</b>. Follow the relay from each of the opponent’s pits and check the empty pit where it stops and the pile opposite.</p><p>Defend as in Kalah: <b>move the pile</b>, <b>fill the landing pit</b>, or <b>change the opponent’s counts</b>.</p>',
